## Survival building blocks

common-items-blocks-dirt = Dirt Block
    .desc = A clump of packed earth. Good for filling holes, or digging new ones.

common-items-blocks-turf = Turf Block
    .desc = Earth with its grass still attached. Makes a lawn wherever it lands.

common-items-blocks-sand = Sand Block
    .desc = Fine, dry sand. Every beach house starts with one.

common-items-blocks-snow = Snow Block
    .desc = Firmly packed snow. Keeps its shape surprisingly well.

common-items-blocks-stone = Stone Block
    .desc = A rough chunk of bedrock. Needs a pickaxe to cut free.

common-items-blocks-timber = Timber Block
    .desc = A section of tree trunk, bark and all.

common-items-blocks-leaves = Leaf Block
    .desc = A dense bundle of leaves. Light, green and a little rustly.

common-items-blocks-ice = Ice Block
    .desc = Clear, cold ice. Cutting it cleanly takes a pickaxe.

common-items-blocks-planks = Plank Block
    .desc = Sawn wooden boards, ready to become floors, walls and roofs.

common-items-blocks-stone_bricks = Stone Bricks
    .desc = Squared stone laid in neat courses. The backbone of any sturdy keep.

common-items-blocks-clay_bricks = Clay Bricks
    .desc = Fired red bricks with pale mortar. Warm, homely and hard-wearing.
